{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 64 days after the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D4"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Indigotindisulfonate sodium has been on FDA's shortage list since 2022-08-23 and remains listed as of 2026-10-21, a span of 50 months.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale General and Corvale East carries NDC 81284031505 and is labeled by Provepharm Inc.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label identifies the manufacturing plant as CENEXI (FEI 3007250542) in France.",
      "cites": ["E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1245208 at that plant ended 2022-10-26 and was classified VAI, which occurred 64 days after the shortage was first posted.",
      "cites": ["D4", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier inspections at the same plant include an OAI classification in 2015 and VAI classifications in 2012, 2016, and 2018.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E6", "E7", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 31 units with 7.1 days on hand, while Corvale General holds 64 units with 14.8 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recommended action is to transfer 3 units of the 8 mg/mL, 5 mL presentation from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to about 8 days of supply while Corvale General retains roughly two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    }
  ]
}
